# Explicit grants for new tables

From 2026-10-30 Supabase no longer auto-grants `anon` / `authenticated` / `service_role`
on new tables in `public`. Without a grant, `supabase-js` gets
`42501 permission denied for table ...`. Existing tables keep their grants.

Every migration that creates a table in `public` must, right after `CREATE TABLE`:

1. Enable RLS and add policies (unchanged).
2. Grant only the privileges the app actually uses — never blanket-grant everything.
3. Grant sequence usage if the table has a serial/identity column the client inserts into.

```sql
create table public.case_documents (...);
alter table public.case_documents enable row level security;

grant select, insert, update, delete on public.case_documents to authenticated;
grant select, insert, update, delete on public.case_documents to service_role;
-- grant select on public.case_documents to anon;  -- only if logged-out visitors read it
```

Edge functions using the service-role key still need the `service_role` grant.
